# Gapless fast path, part 3 of 6: the fixed-wait cut cave.
name: gapless-3-delay-cave
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x030514fe
gate: build refuses unless the 26 stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: Entered by the patched BL at module 33's load-start delay
  site (0024) with r0 = 80 (the stock delay argument) and lr = return
  into 0x03088d9c. It touches only caller-saved registers (r1-r3), which
  any call at that site may clobber. On every invocation it snapshots
  the incoming track's rate ([0x030368d8+8], via the literal pool word
  at 0x03051684 installed by 0025) into the state pair's prev-rate word
  (0x030515b4, see 0020), so the comparison is always against the
  immediately preceding track. It returns immediately -- skipping the
  80 ms settle delay -- only when the gate (0022) marked this open as a
  fast-path skip (retained word >= 0x80) AND the new rate equals the
  previous track's rate. In every other case it tail-branches to the
  stock delay_ms at 0x03064944 with r0 and lr untouched, which is
  behaviour-identical to the stock BL it replaces. The cave occupies
  `bx lr` stub slots at 0x030514fe..0x03051517: the reference scan shows
  zero references to the whole range, the preceding slot 0x030514fc is
  the return of a stub function (0x030514fa, itself unreferenced) so
  nothing falls through into the cave, and the first referenced stub
  of the farm, 0x0305151a, plus the slot at 0x03051518, are left
  byte-identical.
expect: 7047704770477047704770477047704770477047704770477047
